#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1131 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "FLIPPED noViolation -> violation by Fix #331 (M3-D18 / M2-D24 bucket 1, owner ruling 2026-08-22): NonEmptyGuardInliner's bare-emptiness arm is RETIRED (Fix #330), so the machine-emitted var_exists guard this scenario used to pin no longer exists; absent = all-missing, empty(X) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports the defect on exactly the rows its other conjuncts select (1 here). If this goes SILENT again, a guard is being injected -- escalate, do not rewrite toward silence. History, before Fix #330: FRESH, DISCRIMINATING (finding SD1131-F1) - the guard-silenced --STRESC-absent boundary. LB has no LBSTRESC column; Requirements.Variables gates only --BLFL (present), so the rule EXECUTES - the machine-emitted var_exists(\"--STRESC\") guard is false -> noViolation, not skipped, although the baseline record trivially lacks a standardized result."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBBLFL   type=Char label="Baseline Flag"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | GLUC | Y
